#
# The compositor owns the display: it configures the framebuffer and maps its
# Frames through the fb component. It is also the only consumer of the USB HID
# component's input interface: it reads the descriptor and the state of each
# device the component serves, and the events arrive on the interface's
# io-channel. An image without the HID component leaves the input import not
# granted and the compositor runs without input.
uses fb_v1 via device compatible "brcm,bcm2708-fb" { configure, address, size, pixel_order, frames }
uses input_v1 via component usb_hid { descriptor, snapshot }
